## Phase 6 — Import GPG Key

This is the step that enables record signing. Without it, `sign_json_data()` silently returns `None`.

```bash
# Export your GPG private key on the host
gpg --export-secret-keys operator01@orp.local > /tmp/orp_operator.gpg

# Import it into the running container's RAM-disk GPG home
cat /tmp/orp_operator.gpg | \
  docker exec -i orp_engine \
  gpg --homedir /dev/shm/gnupg --import

# Verify the key is visible
docker exec orp_engine \
  gpg --homedir /dev/shm/gnupg --list-secret-keys

# Clean up
rm /tmp/orp_operator.gpg
```

> **Important**: `/dev/shm/gnupg` is ephemeral — it lives in RAM and disappears when the container stops. You must re-import the GPG key after every container restart. This is by design (key never touches disk inside the container). A future improvement is auto-importing from a Docker secret in `entrypoint.sh`.

