## 2. Security Model

### Isolation Layers

| Layer | Mechanism | What it prevents |
|---|---|---|
| Network | `internal: true` on backend_net | Containers cannot phone home |
| Ingress | Single port :9443 via nginx | No direct backend access |
| mTLS (browser→nginx) | operator01.p12 | Unauthorised portal access |
| mTLS (engine→immudb) | engine.crt clientAuth | Unauthorised DB writes |
| Secrets | Docker secrets (tmpfs) | Passwords in env vars / logs |
| Users | Non-root containers | Container escape blast radius |
| PKI | Offline CA (network_mode: none) | CA key exposure during issuance |
| Audit | immudb append-only | Tamper-evident record history |

### Secret Inventory

| Secret | Path in container | Used by |
|---|---|---|
| immudb_password | `/run/secrets/immudb_password` | orp-engine |
| immudb_admin_password | `/run/secrets/immudb_admin_password` | immudb (first boot) |
| operator_p12_password | `/run/secrets/operator_p12_password` | pki-init |
| flask_secret_key | `/run/secrets/flask_secret_key` | orp-engine |

### PKI Layout

```
/pki/
├── ca/
│   ├── ca.crt          644  Trust anchor — all services verify against this
│   └── ca.key          600  Root CA private key — never leaves pki-init
├── nginx/
│   ├── nginx.crt       644  nginx server identity (presented to browsers)
│   └── nginx.key       644  nginx private key
├── engine/
│   ├── engine.crt      644  orp-engine client identity (presented to immudb)
│   └── engine.key      644  orp-engine private key
├── immudb/
│   ├── immudb.crt      644  immudb server identity
│   └── immudb.key      644  immudb private key
└── clients/
    ├── operator01.crt  644  Operator certificate
    ├── operator01.key  600  Operator private key
    └── operator01.p12  600  Browser import bundle (cert + key + CA chain)
```

